{"chunk_id": "ddacf340349d", "text": "This section recounts the climax and aftermath of Indra\u2019s battle with the Asura Vritra. After Vritra overwhelms Indra through powerful illusions, the sage Vasishtha restores Indra\u2019s courage, reminding him of the gods and sages watching. Empowered through Yoga, Indra dispels Vritra\u2019s illusions while Vishnu enters Indra\u2019s thunderbolt and Shiva\u2019s energy manifests as a devastating fever that weakens the Asura. As ominous portents appear around Vritra, Indra strikes while the demon yawns under the fever\u2019s grip, killing him with the thunderbolt. Yet the victory brings consequence: the embodied sin of Brahmanicide emerges from Vritra\u2019s corpse and clings to Indra. Terrified, Indra hides for years until Brahma arranges to divide the sin among Agni, plants, Apsaras, and the Waters, establishing ritual and moral rules explaining how that sin transfers to humans.\nIndra slays Vritra with divine aid but is seized by the sin of Brahmanicide, which Brahma later disperses among Agni, plants, Apsaras, and the waters.\nThemes: divine warfare, karma and sin, ritual purity, cosmic justice, divine intervention", "vector": [0.006576249375939369, -0.018431026488542557, -0.0083930604159832, 0.005517847370356321, 0.002143769757822156, 0.027963386848568916, -0.03419245406985283, -0.013455863110721111, -0.006862759590148926, -0.01442662626504898, 0.0050088707357645035, 0.01481762807816267, 0.012552512809634209, 0.008062731474637985, -0.0034819403663277626, 0.0070110708475112915, 0.04203945770859718, -0.006805457640439272, 0.03910020366311073, -0.025226371362805367, -0.003428009105846286, 0.005588632542639971, 0.00010027853568317369, 0.026507239788770676, -0.015774909406900406, -0.0039605810306966305, 0.012222183868288994, -0.02395898662507534, 0.004176306072622538, -0.008898667059838772, -0.0029813903383910656, -0.0009286298300139606, -0.00116542202886194, -0.0012791833141818643, -0.01011212170124054, 0.00047948307474143